---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout currentPage="consulting">
  <div class="consulting-content">
    <p>
      I'm a founding engineer at Falconer, where I build production AI agent systems — tool
      execution, retrieval pipelines, evals, and streaming at scale. Before that, staff engineer
      at Stripe. MIT EECS. I take on a small number of consulting engagements on the side.
    </p>
    <p>
      Most of what I see go wrong: teams build rigid workflow pipelines that break the moment users
      go off-script. The better approach is a general agentic loop with well-designed tools — the
      model is good enough to figure out what to call and in what order. Evals built on the happy path are mostly useless
      too; the signal is in the failure cases, and end-to-end evals catch things that
      component-level evals never will. Don't optimize for model cost early either — build on the
      best available model, ship something that works, and find the cheaper paths later.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm most useful when the question is around agent architecture, eval design, tool design, or
      getting something from demo to production — including building an end-to-end prototype in a
      new area if that's what you need to figure out if something is worth pursuing.
      <a href="mailto:consulting@kyeb.com">Get in touch</a> if any of that sounds useful.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .consulting-content {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .consulting-content p {
    font-weight: 300;
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
  }

  .consulting-content a {
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--link);
    padding-bottom: 1px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--link-underline);
  }

  .consulting-content a:hover {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--link);
  }
</style>
